# Observability Lab: MELT Telemetry Data Triage & Framework Analysis

## 1. Incident Overview & Operational Scope

Incident `INC-84920` was a SEV-1 production outage affecting the `checkout-service` in the E-Commerce Checkout & Payment Platform. The incident started at `14:02:15 UTC` immediately after version `v2.4.1` was deployed and was resolved at `14:20:30 UTC`, lasting approximately 18.25 minutes.

During the incident, checkout P99 latency increased from a normal level of approximately 215–228 ms to a peak of 6450 ms. The checkout HTTP error rate increased from approximately 0.12–0.15% to 22.40%. Checkout throughput dropped from 435 requests per second to 260 requests per second.

The outage was caused by a database connection leak in the new loyalty discount module. The leaked connections exhausted the 50-connection HikariCP database pool, causing requests to wait for connections and eventually fail with HTTP 500 errors.

The incident was resolved by rolling back `checkout-service` from version `v2.4.1` to the stable version `v2.4.0`.

