## 2. MELT Telemetry Classification Matrix

| Signal Description | MELT Classification (Metric / Event / Log / Trace) | Primary Data Format / Structure | Key Characteristics (Aggregation / Context / Breadth) | Storage & Retention Trade-off (Low / Med / High Cost) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| HTTP 500 error rate percentage over time | Metric | Numeric time-series data | Aggregated percentage, low individual-request context, broad service-health visibility | Low |
| Deployment rollout completed notification (`v2.4.1`) | Event | Structured timestamped event record with metadata | Records a discrete state change with deployment version, image and rollout status | Low |
| Distributed request span waterfall (`/api/v1/checkout`) | Trace | Parent-child span hierarchy with timestamps, durations and tags | Provides detailed request flow across services, high context and request-level visibility | High |
| Stack trace: `SQLTransientConnectionException` | Log | Timestamped structured textual record containing exception details | Detailed application context, exception class, root-cause message and source location | Medium |
| P99 response latency time series | Metric | Numeric time-series data | Aggregated percentile measurement showing service performance over time | Low |
| Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler scaling from 5 to 10 replicas | Event | Structured timestamped event with scaling metadata | Discrete infrastructure state change containing previous and new replica counts | Low |
| HikariCP connection acquisition latency warning message | Log | Timestamped textual record with severity and execution context | Contains request-level context such as thread, trace ID and measured connection wait time | Medium |
| Database connection pool active connection count (`50/50`) | Metric | Numeric time-series gauge | Aggregated resource-utilization measurement showing pool saturation | Low |
| Parent-child span hierarchy linking Gateway, Checkout and DB | Trace | Distributed trace containing linked spans and parent span IDs | End-to-end request visibility across service boundaries with detailed latency attribution | High |
| Prometheus alert rule firing (`CheckoutServiceHighLatencyP99`) | Event | Structured alert event containing threshold and observed value | Discrete operational occurrence that records when a monitoring condition was triggered | Low |

